  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "⚔️ LOTR Orc Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Orcs of Mordor, Isengard and the Misty Mountains, in the sound of Tolkien's Black Speech."
    },
    "intro": "Tolkien's <a href=\"orc-name-generator.html\">orcs</a> have some of the best names in the book: Shagrat, Gorbag, Uglúk, Grishnákh. Short, ugly and memorable, and nearly always given to an orc who's about to fall out with another orc. This **LOTR orc name generator** builds names with the same sounds, and can add a rank or the place your orc serves: the Tower, the White Hand, Gundabad.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The Black Speech",
        "content": "<p>Sauron devised the Black Speech for his servants, and the Ring's inscription is the best-known line of it: <em>Ash nazg durbatulûk</em>, \"one ring to rule them all\". A few words are clear enough to borrow:</p><ul><li><strong>nazg</strong>, ring, as in the Nazgûl, the Ring-wraiths.</li><li><strong>uruk</strong>, orc. The Uruk-hai are the \"orc-folk\".</li><li><strong>snaga</strong>, slave: what the big orcs call the small ones.</li><li><strong>ghâsh</strong>, fire, and <strong>Lugbúrz</strong>, the orcs' name for Barad-dûr, the Dark Tower.</li></ul><p>Tolkien also wrote that orcs of different tribes could barely understand each other's dialects, so they used the Common Speech among themselves. That's why their names are a mix: some Black Speech, some just ugly.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Tolkien's orcs and their names",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Shagrat</strong>, captain of the Tower of Cirith Ungol, and <strong>Gorbag</strong> of Minas Morgul, who fight over Frodo's mithril shirt.</li><li><strong>Uglúk</strong>, leader of Saruman's Uruk-hai, and <strong>Grishnákh</strong>, the Mordor orc who tries to steal the <a href=\"hobbit-name-generator.html\">hobbits</a> for himself.</li><li><strong>Azog</strong> and his son <strong>Bolg</strong>, <a href=\"goblin-name-generator.html\">goblins</a> of the Misty Mountains, and <strong>Golfimbul</strong>, whose head Bandobras Took knocked off with a club, inventing golf.</li></ul><p>None of these are in the generator, so your orc won't be confused with one of them.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Three kinds of orc",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Mordor orcs</strong> serve Sauron directly, from the Tower, the Black Gate and the vale of Udûn.</li><li><strong>Uruk-hai of Isengard</strong> are Saruman's: bigger, stronger, unafraid of the sun, and loud about it. They carry the White Hand.</li><li><strong>Goblins of the Misty Mountains</strong> live in tunnels at Gundabad, Moria and Goblin-town. In <em>The Hobbit</em> Tolkien calls them goblins; it's the same creature.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Using the name",
        "content": "<ul><li><strong>Role-play and tabletop</strong>: The One Ring and other Middle-earth games are full of orcs who need names quickly. Generate a batch before the session.</li><li><strong>Video games</strong>: Shadow of Mordor's Nemesis captains are named in this style, with titles; the rank format is a good fit for your own.</li><li><strong>Fan fiction</strong>: give your orc a rank and a grudge. Tolkien's orcs are at their best when they're arguing.</li></ul>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What's the difference between Mordor orcs, Uruk-hai and goblins?",
        "answer": "Mordor orcs serve Sauron; the Uruk-hai are Saruman's larger orcs from Isengard, who can march in daylight; goblins are the orcs of the Misty Mountains, called goblins in The Hobbit. Pick the kind and the rank and place will suit."
      },
      {
        "question": "Why do some names have û or á?",
        "answer": "Tolkien used accents to mark long vowels, and you'll see them in Black Speech words like Lugbúrz and durbatulûk. A few of the names here use them the same way."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are these names from the books?",
        "answer": "No. They're built from Black Speech-style sounds, and the names of Tolkien's own orcs are left out."
      },
      {
        "question": "Can I use these names in my game or story?",
        "answer": "Yes, they're free to use and you don't need to credit the site."
      }
    ]
  }
